1
00:00:00,495 --> 00:00:02,419
Your cat has never tasted sugar.

2
00:00:02,626 --> 00:00:03,895
Not once in its whole life.

3
00:00:04,114 --> 00:00:06,133
And it's not because you never shared your

4
00:00:05,983 --> 00:00:06,538
dessert.

5
00:00:06,781 --> 00:00:08,990
Its body simply can't detect sweet.

6
00:00:09,628 --> 00:00:11,850
To taste something sweet, your tongue needs a

7
00:00:11,700 --> 00:00:14,409
special receptor built from two genes.

8
00:00:14,664 --> 00:00:16,814
Cats have both genes, but one of them

9
00:00:16,676 --> 00:00:17,469
is broken.

10
00:00:18,095 --> 00:00:20,579
In two thousand five, scientists found the bug:

11
00:00:20,905 --> 00:00:23,138
a small piece of that gene is missing,

12
00:00:23,381 --> 00:00:25,102
so the receptor never gets built.

13
00:00:25,393 --> 00:00:27,567
For a cat, sugar tastes like nothing.

14
00:00:27,798 --> 00:00:28,519
Let's level up.

15
00:00:29,116 --> 00:00:29,802
Level one:

16
00:00:30,176 --> 00:00:31,207
why it doesn't matter.

17
00:00:31,438 --> 00:00:34,362
Cats are pure carnivores, and meat has almost

18
00:00:34,212 --> 00:00:35,076
no sugar.

19
00:00:35,295 --> 00:00:37,802
So when the sweet gene broke, cats lost

20
00:00:37,664 --> 00:00:38,302
nothing.

21
00:00:38,928 --> 00:00:40,078
And it's not just your cat.

22
00:00:40,321 --> 00:00:43,150
Tigers and cheetahs have the exact same broken

23
00:00:43,000 --> 00:00:43,483
gene.

24
00:00:43,726 --> 00:00:45,626
The whole family lost its sweet tooth.

25
00:00:46,250 --> 00:00:46,984
Level two:

26
00:00:47,357 --> 00:00:48,329
the meat detector.

27
00:00:48,560 --> 00:00:51,674
Instead of sweet, cats are experts at umami,

28
00:00:51,953 --> 00:00:53,555
the savory taste of meat.

29
00:00:53,798 --> 00:00:56,805
And tuna is packed with the exact molecules

30
00:00:56,667 --> 00:00:57,555
that trigger it.

31
00:00:58,195 --> 00:00:59,726
That's why the sound of a can opening

32
00:00:59,588 --> 00:01:02,238
turns your cat into a heat-seeking missile.

33
00:01:02,850 --> 00:01:03,619
Level three:

34
00:01:03,910 --> 00:01:05,012
the poison shield.

35
00:01:05,255 --> 00:01:07,607
Cats have only about four hundred and seventy

36
00:01:07,457 --> 00:01:08,465
taste buds.

37
00:01:08,707 --> 00:01:10,072
We have around nine thousand.

38
00:01:10,315 --> 00:01:12,310
But they can still detect bitter, which helps

39
00:01:12,172 --> 00:01:14,953
them avoid spoiled food and some poisons.

40
00:01:15,595 --> 00:01:17,031
Now, the final boss:

41
00:01:17,048 --> 00:01:19,055
but my cat loves ice cream!

42
00:01:19,298 --> 00:01:20,257
Here's the twist.

43
00:01:20,500 --> 00:01:21,495
It's not the sugar.

44
00:01:21,738 --> 00:01:23,626
It's most likely the fat and the milk

45
00:01:23,476 --> 00:01:24,483
proteins.

46
00:01:25,128 --> 00:01:27,921
And many adult cats are lactose intolerant.

47
00:01:28,152 --> 00:01:29,969
So that scoop of ice cream can end

48
00:01:29,819 --> 00:01:31,623
with a very unhappy stomach.

49
00:01:32,274 --> 00:01:33,603
So next time your cat stares at your

50
00:01:33,465 --> 00:01:35,484
cookie, it's not craving sugar.

51
00:01:35,703 --> 00:01:37,222
It just wants to know if there's any

52
00:01:37,072 --> 00:01:37,781
meat in it.

53
00:01:38,428 --> 00:01:40,090
Would your cat trade a cake for a

54
00:01:39,952 --> 00:01:40,709
can of tuna?

55
00:01:40,940 --> 00:01:42,031
Tell me in the comments.
